From 88b6a6c3d101ea4a3f21320020dda91dc2a3be27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel <kernel@local>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:04:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Kernel hipx14 ported to v1.1.75

hipx14 (IK2_ABLATE, IK2_KV=q4, IK2_HIP_* switches; all default off) on top of
v1.1.75, conflicts resolved keeping upstream's behaviour:
- rms_row (ours) under upstream's rms_impl_row / rms_impl_jobs_kernel;
  proj_out_kernel kept
- attn_decode_mma_kernel: upstream's window/streaming params (blk0, tok_*,
  share_T) + the q4 fragments; combine: upstream's per-token z offsets +
  IK2_HIP_COMB's B template
- attn_decode_mma_impl: blk0/nblk/phase + q4 Volta abort + COMB
- lg_launch: IK2_HIP_LGD/NT on AMD, upstream's loop_gate_dots_toks on CUDA
- STRATA_USE_HIP -> MAYA_USE_HIP (upstream rename; the HIP switches were
  silently compiled out otherwise)
- CUDA build: __builtin_amdgcn_sched_barrier / __builtin_nontemporal_load
  shimmed (the HIP-only paths are dead code there)
New 1.1.75 paths:
- q4 in attn_decode_mma_win_kernel + attn_decode_mma_toks_q4 (the exact
  verify window's tokens kernel), main's toks branch takes it
- IK2_ABLATE in the verify window's MoE: proj_conv with ys (the token
  path's one block of 1024 - each token's output the token path's bits)
- --parallel: q4 slot caches, q4 attention, ablation of wo and MoE rows,
  embd_host for the rows' embeddings
- two GPUs: router logits before two_send (no FUSE there)
- KV streaming off with q4; KV lending / IK2_DEPTH / VRAM lines with
  kv_row_bytes; Volta prompt attention (pa70) off with q4
